  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that, among RNA-only single-profile models, scvi_n200 is the strongest representation (accuracy 0.520, F1 0.498), while pca_n2000 and scgpt are weaker. There is no evidence yet for multiprofile settings. config_005 tests whether multiple profiles with a simple avgpool aggregation improve over the best single-profile RNA model while keeping the RNA encoder fixed and avoiding more complex choices like transformer aggregation or multimodal fusion. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising RNA representation, isolates the profile/aggregation question with minimal added complexity, and will clarify whether multiprofile modeling is worth further investment before testing fusion or image modalities."
